message.content:
Below is a simple example of an HTML “card” that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the dimensions, colors, or animation speed to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
  /* Container that holds the card */
  .card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
  }

  /* The card itself */
  .card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D transforms */
    position: relative;
  }

  /* Front side of the card */
  .card::before,
  .card::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;     /* Hide backside while rotating */
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .card::before {
    background: #4CAF50;            /* Front face color */
    color: white;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  }

  /* Back side of the card */
  .card::after {
    background: #2196F3;            /* Back face color */
    color: white;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);      /* Start rotated so it's hidden */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  }

  /* Hover effect – rotate the card 180° */
  .card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front content -->
    <div class="front">Front Side</div>
    <!-- Back content -->
    <div class="back">Back Side</div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` has `perspective: 1000px;` to give a realistic 3D depth effect.
2. **Card container** – The `.card` element uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its children maintain 3D positioning.
3. **Front & Back faces** – The pseudo‑elements `::before` and `::after` represent the front and back sides.  
   - The back side is initially rotated 180° (`rotateY(180deg)`) so it’s hidden.
4. **Hover** – When hovering over `.card`, we rotate it 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side.

You can replace the text inside the `.front` and `.back` divs with images, icons, or any other content you like. Enjoy!
